On Tue, 28 Feb 2006 06:06:06 +0100, Eric Bohm <bohm@gate.csgeeks.org>  
wrote:

> Trying to adapt my playing style from nethack (where I have ascended
> every class, and an atheist) with limited success.
>
> My Wizard made it down to Medusa, but I stupidly failed to blindfold
> myself.  I tried some rogues who made it past the class quest. But fell
> to nasty things in the alignment quests like Vecna.  Lost characters to
> the nasty tricks in the chaos quest (priest, arch lich, mind flayers,
> Nightmare etc).  Switched to undead slayers so I could see some new
> class quests.

Vecna is a *big* trouble. Usually, I don't do the chaotic quest before  
genociding L, and sometimes also V for safety. But Vecna alone is already  
a lot of trouble. Usual recommendations is scroll of earth + automatic gun  
+ +6/+7 bullets. Or usual potion of paralysis/ring of free action trick.  
I'll rate him second only to Demogorgon in decreasing order of difficulty.

> Recently the common denominator problem has been mages summoning
> unbelievable amounts of stuff.  My gnomish undead slayers invariably
> come up against vampire mages in graveyards (too deep in to take out
> quickly) who soon fill the dungeon with potent monsters.  A few umber
> hulks, minotaurs, and dragons along with an undead army and your day is
> in serious trouble if you're only 14th level and still a hell of a long
> way from a full ascension kit.

Right. In the chaotic quest, stay close to the portal and let them come.  
And go away when things start to be bad. But that is not always enough...  
Knowing charm monster/command undead (try a necromancer, they're funny in  
the chaotic quest when they end up with ~20 pet vampires...) helps. Or  
confuse scroll of taming.

> I haven't been lucky enough to stumble on any wands of wishing.  Which
> typically means I may luck into one wish per game from a throne,
> fountain, lamp, or gypsy.  The Gods of slashem seem substantially less
> generous.  In my last game my best weapon was a stack of enchanted
> silver daggers.  Since god only gave me giant killer (mostly useless).
> Several of my characters would have been terribly equipt without the
> gnomish tinker ability.

Potions of gain levels are not so hard to alchemise. Getting enough of  
them to have magic whistle + BoH is among my first prioity (usually in the  
mines for the whistle and just after Soko for the BoH). Then, make enough  
to turn all these cloaks/boots/gloves/... into the ones you want.

> Kudos on Dracula by the way, totally wiped the walls with me.  Seems
> like I may have to fort up to take him down.  Either that or somehow end
> up facing him with a stack of magic silver bullets and an assault rifle.
>  Silver bullets don't seem to be in generous supply so I don't know if
> that will ever happen.

Bullets, on the other hand, are fairly common given the amount of soldiers  
(in the orcish stronghold if not elsewhere). And frag grenades are nice  
too (but heavy). Enchanting a stack of bullet up to +6/+7 is quite easy,  
there are usually plenty of enchantment scrolls.

You may also want to try playing some of the easier combination.  
Doppelgagner monk is quite nice. Slash'em monk are much more powerful than  
nethack's and doppelganger #youpoly is very strong (turn into a basilisk  
and get several nice pets, plus your stoning attack...) (or turn into a  
crystal golem... but this don't work against Vecna).

And overall: beware of the chaotic quest. You don't *need* to do it (you  
need to do only two of the aligned quest, the neutral one is very easy,  
the lawful one is a bit painsul if the Spice girls are still there...) Of  
course, getting the hand of Vecna is nice but being alive is better.



